WEBVTT

1
00:02.500 --> 00:11.000
Introducing the Workbench, for Grok Build. We love Grok. We love Linux. We just don't love living in the terminal.

2
00:11.000 --> 00:20.000
So we built a window onto Grok Build, for people who'd rather vibe-code than type. Here's what that looks like.

3
00:21.000 --> 00:32.000
You tell the agent what you want, and it starts thinking. But before it changes a single file, it stops and asks, in its own words.

4
00:32.000 --> 00:44.000
You read it, click Yes, and only then does it write the file. That little line? That's what it cost. Nothing changes your files until you say so.

5
00:44.500 --> 00:55.000
The agent just made three changes. This drawer lists every file it touched, with the real count of lines added and removed, nothing guessed.

6
00:55.000 --> 01:10.000
Open one and see it before and after, side by side. Don't like this change? Click Undo. It tells you in plain words what that will do, you confirm, and that one change is gone, the other two stay put.

7
01:10.000 --> 01:26.000
And here's the part that matters most: if you edited that file yourself, undoing the agent's work never touches what you wrote. Your work stays yours.

8
01:27.000 --> 01:42.000
This meter shows how full the agent's working memory is right now, and the numbers actually add up, because we checked. Feeling crowded? Click Compact to clear space, and watch the real number drop.

9
01:42.000 --> 01:55.000
Below that, your privacy settings sit next to where each one comes from. And the only switch that shares more of your data always asks you first.

10
01:56.000 --> 02:11.000
Now watch us kill the agent mid-sentence, on purpose, for real. No blank screen, no fake "everything's fine." A plain red line tells you exactly what happened: the agent was killed.

11
02:11.000 --> 02:25.000
Then the app reloads every session from the files saved on your machine, marks it recovered, and the next question answers fine. Still here.

12
02:26.000 --> 02:35.000
Every session on your machine, together in one list, grouped by folder. Open a second one alongside it. Rename this one right where it sits.

13
02:35.000 --> 02:43.000
Fold a group and keep the count. Run several at once, everything in one place.

14
02:44.000 --> 02:55.000
So that's the Workbench, for Grok Build. It doesn't change what the agent can do, it makes what it already does easy to see, and easy to use.

15
02:55.000 --> 03:08.000
Browse for a file instead of typing out the path. Start a session, and find it again later. Rename your work, undo any change, and always know where your privacy settings stand.

16
03:08.000 --> 03:17.000
The Workbench runs on your own machine, it collects nothing itself, and it's free and open source. We made Grok Build easier to build with. That's the Workbench. For Grok Build.